    page('Track H: real database portfolios and maintenance cost',p('SQLite holds 200,000 synthetic bookings, 20,000 customers and 600 stations. Binary index choices maximize measured training benefit under a B-tree storage budget. Greedy gain/KiB and ILP compare with the default planner and all-index reference. All 64 candidate subsets certify the finite surrogate model.'),t(['Portfolio','Index MiB','Held-out ms','Mixed QPS','Insert rows/s'],[[r['label'],f"{r['index_mib']:.3f}",f"{r['weighted_heldout_ms']:.3f}",f"{r['median_qps']:.0f}",f"{r['median_insert_rows_per_s']:.0f}"] for r in h],[.30,.16,.18,.16,.20]),im('tracks/H/results/figures/latency.png','Same held-out SQL/parameters; throughput is independently timed from mixed batches.',165),p('At 60% ILP, mixed-read QPS is 33.11x baseline, using 12.777 MiB indexes while insertion throughput falls from about 103,371 to 18,727 rows/s. This optimizes a read objective, not all operations.'),p('Raw EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN records are high-level plans, not invented EXPLAIN ANALYZE counters. Independent references preserve integers, NULL behavior, ordering and LIMIT ties. The model certificate does not prove arbitrary-index or future-runtime optimality. Seventeen retained host tests pass.'),ev('tracks/H/results/model.json; selections.json; plans.json; latency_runs.json; write_runs.json'))
